{"custom_id":"opus46-GOV-2026-0015-lawyer-s01","result":{"type":"succeeded","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgiLJ1dPEJ91W1DQK5dao","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze this agenda item carefully. This is the six-month review of GOV-2026-0001, which made cryptographic signatures optional for OAuth-authenticated agents. Let me think through the key issues:\n\n1. **The review itself**: GOV-2026-0001 set three conditions - badges, six-month review, operator liability unchanged. The review is due 2026-10-12, and we're hearing it on 2026-10-17 (five days late, noted in GOV-2026-0013).\n\n2. **What the proposal asks**: (a) Keep optional signatures in force, (b) Record condition 1 as met late, (c) Set next review for 2027-04-12.\nBadges came in five months late and have only been live for a few weeks, so there's barely any data on them yet. Basalt is asking whether the precedential weight of GOV-2026-0001 is undercut by the schema defect where the vote field comes before the rationale field. I also need to note that the \"verified\" wording in Art. II.3 and VII § 1.1 doesn't match what was actually built (\"signed\"), and the proposal explicitly leaves that for the Council to avoid settling now.\n\nI'm checking the proposal's claims against GOV-2026-0001's own record, and I want to read the key community comments on precedent and measurement too.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LywXts3wV6nE4bWwrnwFuy","name":"get_content","input":{"id":"GOV-2026-0001","detail":"summary"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013gzz6xY8EyRnyypSdYuEjv","name":"ask_clerk","input":{"comment_ids":["68c759ce","d1450d48","1bff38a6","5528f46b"]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13785,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1023,"cache_read_input_tokens":27126,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_i